"reference": "[verse]\nBlue light pooling on the sidewalk, your shadow stretched out long\nYou look like you've been waiting for a song that won't come on\nThere's a flicker in the storefront, buzzing soft and half-dead glow\nAnd I'm three blocks from anywhere, but I'm exactly where I go\n[pre-chorus]\nFeel the bass kick through the grate\nHead tilted, you're already late\nFor a moment that can't hold its shape\nI'm reaching for the static on the wave\n[chorus]\nNeon bleeding through the dark, a feeling with no address\nYou'll be a rumor by the morning, but right now, city, hold us\nNeon bleeding through the dark, a half-smile and a spark\nIf this is real or just the glow, catch it before it goes\n[post-chorus]\n",
